610                                                       |
The value of input Q361 Laser beam axis is incorrect. The
value of Q361 can only be 1 (X axis) or 0 (Y axis).
611                                                       |
The value of input Q374 Measurement side for profiling is
incorrect.
612                                                       |
The value of input Q365/ROFFS Radial step over exceeds the
maximum tool radius set in the Renishaw set-up table.
613                                                       |
The value of input Q362 Measuring direction is incorrect.
The value of Q362 can only be +1 (positive direction), -1
(negative direction), or 0 (both).
614                                                       |

615                                                       |
At least one measurement in the sample is outside the
scatter tolerance limit, defined by scatter tolerance in the
Renishaw set-up table. The alarm will arise once the number
of retries (double the number of final touches) has been
exceeded.
616                                                       |
The tool setting system is not active and/or responding
(Renishaw alarm).
617                                                       |
The active tool length exceeds the maximum tool length
specified in the Renishaw set-up table.
618                                                       |
The active tool length is less than the minimum tool length
specified in the Renishaw set-up table.
619                                                       |
The active tool radius exceeds the maximum tool radius
specified in the Renishaw set-up table.
620                                                       |
The active tool is out of tolerance. This alarm arises in
the broken tool detection cycle (506) if the measured
dimension of the tool is outside the input LBREAK tolerance
for that cycle. In this circumstance, the Tool Lock (TL) is
applied to the active tool in the tool table.
621                                                       |
The receiver has not registered a beam cut condition during
the measure move, possibly because:
* the tool is missing,
* in the alignment cycle (500 or 501), the tool is 
  pre-positioned excessively far from the beam,
* its approximate length (where required) in the tool table 
  is incorrectly short.
* the NC system has been significantly moved since
  calibration.
622                                                       |
The active tool is out of tolerance. This alarm arises in
the tool profile checking cycle (508) and cutting edge
checking cycle (510) if the measured dimension of the tool
cutting edge is outside the input RBREAK cutting edge
tolerance for that cycle. This can be due, in part or
exclusively, to eccentricity / runout of the tool. In these 
circumstances the Tool Lock (TL) is applied to the active
tool in the tool table.
623                                                       |
The receiver is registering a beam-cut signal at the start
of a measuring move. This may be due to the tool, swarf or
coolant interfering with the beam.
624                                                       |

625                                                       |
The selected cycle is not supported by the hardware
installation. This alarm usually arises if an extended cycle
(cutter profile checking [508] and cutting edge checking
[510]) is selected, without the necessary machine inputs or
M-code having been assigned or connected.
626                                                       |

627                                                       |
The value of input Q365/ROFFS radial step over exceeds the
active tool radius defined in the tool table.
628                                                       |
The value of input Q371 (cutter height) exceeds the maximum
value allowed (item 42 in the Renishaw set-up table).
629                                                       |
The active tool is out of tolerance. This alarm arises in
the setting/checking cycles (503, 504 and 505) if the
measured dimension of the tool is outside the relevant tool
table LTOL / RTOL tolerance values. In this circumstance,
the Tool Lock (TL) is applied to the active tool in the tool
table.
NOTE: If the input Q380 (1) is used, then the relevant DL
/ DR tool wear registers will have been adjusted, showing
the error amounts from nominal.
630                                                       |
This is a diagnostic message that is displayed at the end of
the SysTest.h system test program. It indicates that the
Renishaw system test is successful.
